      "side": 1,
      "message": "I have to walk back the above statement, it was reporting the min level correctly but it doesn\u0027t resolve the bug - the change in vndk.go is checking if:\n\napiLevel (which is \u0027UpsideDownCake\u0027) is less than \u0027minApiForArch\u0027 (which, after the proposed patch, would be ApiLevelFromUser(ctx, \u0027current\u0027), which is just \u0027current\u0027 again.\n\nThe underlying problem again would be that we\u0027re comparing a preview codename to a preview API level, which would fail the comparison and still reject the bundling of the vNDK.",
