      "writtenOn": "2023-03-16T04:59:46Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The `len(targets) \u003e 0` is just to ensure the `targets[0]` doesn\u0027t trigger a nil pointer dereference.  It is checking the list of targets supported by the current apex version, e.g. `[riscv64]` or `[arm64, arm]`.  riscv64 is 64-bit only, most x86_64 and arm64 builds also support x86 or arm, but we also have arm64-only builds without arm.\n\nI think the build won\u0027t fail if you remove all this code because we currently build with `ALLOW_MISSING_DEPENDENCIES\u003dtrue`, but I added it because that hack will need to be turned off eventually.\n\nTry adding `vndkVersion !\u003d mctx.DeviceConfig().PlatformVndkVersion()` to the list of checks on line 79.",
      "parentUuid": "373b0787_f642e92b",
      "revId": "9f50668d13501f5873fc1c7f5f17ab5ea0f90ef1",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
